reasons={5:['The characteristic polynomial is (s+3)^2, so the repeated negative pole is critically damped.','Total stiffness 16 requires k_p=15; total critical damping is 2 sqrt(4*16)=16, so k_v=15.','The speed-generated back EMF is k_e omega; terminal voltage additionally supplies the resistive and inductive drops.','The stated factor-of-two bound gives omega_n at most40 rad/s, but it is not a full stability proof.','Substitution of u=x^3+v cancels the exact modeled nonlinearity, leaving x double-dot=v.','The forces are20N and80N, so their ratio is4; the two stiffness coefficients have different units.','Identity scaling and a zero offset pass the explicitly torque-level command through unchanged.','The repeated-root response is (0.1+0.3t)exp(-3t), which satisfies the equation and both initial conditions.','The matched joint coordinates and their first two derivatives give position, velocity and acceleration errors.','Virtual power requires tau=J-transpose F=(3,10); inverse and non-transposed maps are different.'],6:['Arbitrary mixed-unit numerical scales can change Euclidean neighbours; the metric and scaling must reflect intended similarity.','Numerically encoded category labels remain classification targets.','Known labels supervise DatasetA; DatasetB groups unlabeled samples by similarity.','The graph has two free input coordinates and is an affine plane of codimension one in R3, hence also a hyperplane.','fit estimates coefficients; predict applies them, score evaluates and get_params inspects configuration.','A single object dtype can reference both an integer and a string; DataFrame columns can have different dtypes.','The unweighted mean90/5=18 minimizes squared constant-leaf loss.','The point follows false at x1<=10 and true at x2<=5, reaching the leaf with mean14.','A policy specifies action choices or their probabilities, not reward, value or state-transition dynamics.','Nonterminal target12 yields4.8; terminal target3 with no bootstrap yields3.9.']}
flags={5:{3:'The answer is correct, but the complete armature voltage equation used by the question and solution is absent from the cited assignment item. Add the actual premise on lecture physical675, printed7, which explicitly gives L di/dt+Ri=V-k_e omega; preserve assignmentp20 as the original item locator.',7:'The answer is correct under the supplied pass-through definition, but the stem calls tau=alpha*u+beta the source decomposition while the two cited assignment pages only give alpha/beta choices. Either label that decomposition an explicitly added definition or add its exact lecture premise; retain the torque-level qualification.'},6:{4:'The pre-answer stem explicitly calls plane and hyperplane overlapping choices, which reveals the relationship being tested. Remove that conclusion from the stem and keep it in the solution; preserve the explicit two-independent-input graph scope.'}}
